-- title:
--   Two-chart coordinates from a section of 𝒪(mε)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian local commutative ring, and let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes that is proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral. Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, that is, a morphism $\varepsilon_1 : \operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $c$ equal to the identity; write $\mathcal{I} =$ `ε.1.ker` for the kernel ideal sheaf data of $\varepsilon_1$. Let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number, and let $s$ be a morphism from the unit object of $C$-modules to $(\mathcal{I}^m)$`.invModule`, the dual $\underline{\operatorname{Hom}}(\,\cdot\,,\mathbf{1})$ of the module associated with $\mathcal{I}^m$ (the latter being the kernel of the unit-to-pushforward-unit map of the corresponding closed immersion); so $s$ is a global section of $\mathcal{O}(m\varepsilon)$. Assume that no point of the image of the underlying map of $\varepsilon_1$ lies in the support of `zeroSchemeIdeal s`, the infimum of those ideal sheaf data $J$ with $\operatorname{span}(\operatorname{range}(\mathrm{coeff}\,s\,U)) \le J(U)$ for every affine open $U$. Then there are opens $U, V \subseteq C$ with $U \sqcup V = \top$, such that $U$ consists exactly of the points outside the image of $\varepsilon_1$ and $V$ of the points outside the support of `zeroSchemeIdeal s`, together with sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$ and $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$ satisfying $U \cap V = C_f = C_g$ (basic opens), such that the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \cap V$ have product $1$, and such that for every affine open $W \le V$ the ideal of $\mathcal{I}^m$ at $W$ is generated by the restriction of $g$ to $W$.
--
--   This is the two-chart description of a curve equipped with a section and a section of $\mathcal{O}(m\varepsilon)$ vanishing nowhere along $\varepsilon$: the curve is covered by the complement of the section and the complement of the zero scheme of $s$, with mutually inverse coordinates on the overlap and with the second coordinate generating the $m$-th power of the ideal sheaf of $\varepsilon$ locally on $V$. It is the sheaf-theoretic interface used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_of_section_invModule`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_of_section_invModule) in the construction of Weierstrass-type data for such curves.
